				1023,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Compact function signatures in UI service handlers\n\nCollapse multi-line function parameter definitions into single lines for `QuickInputShowQuickPick`, `QuickInputShowInputBox`, and `WorkspacesRemoveFolder` in the `WindServiceHandlers` module. Remove unnecessary line breaks and adjust indentation to align with the project's compact style preference for standard Rust function signatures, while preserving the internal formatting of complex argument processing logic.\n\nThis change reduces visual noise in the IPC handler definitions without altering behavior or breaking the strict PascalCase naming conventions for arguments and types.",
			"SHA": "d504e17d3070588332dcd56451f0d2a14e0705eb"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T06:32:46Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1023,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement extension metadata and configuration gRPC handlers\n\nIntroduce three new RPC handlers in the `CocoonService` to fulfill the extension management contract defined in the `Vine` protocol:\n\n- `GetAllExtensions`: Iterates over scanned extensions and projects their metadata (Identifier, Name, Version, Location) into `ExtensionInfo` DTOs, defaulting `is_active` to true for discovered items.\n- `GetExtension`: Resolves a single extension by ID, returning its manifest details or `None` if not found.\n- `GetConfiguration`: Resolves workspace configuration values for the requesting extension by composing `section.key` strings, serializing the result to JSON bytes, and handling missing keys gracefully.\n\nThese handlers utilize the `CommonLibrary::ExtensionManagement` traits for data retrieval and adhere to the project's PascalCase naming conventions and `ActionEffect`-style error mapping patterns.",
			"SHA": "774e4c78701f28151f7921cc26142fa2803aa955"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T06:32:39Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1019,
				11
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement core gRPC file system handlers for Cocoon\n\nIntroduce the complete set of file system operations required by the Cocoon extension host, defined in the Vine protocol and implemented within the Mountain backend's `RPC::CocoonService`.\n\nAdd handlers for standard file operations: `CopyFile`, `CreateDirectory`, `DeleteFile`, `Readdir`, `RenameFile`, `Stat`, `ReadFile`, `WriteFile`, `FindFiles`, `FindTextInFiles`, and `WatchFile`. The implementation converts incoming URIs to native `PathBuf` objects, handles parent directory creation where necessary, and respects workspace roots for search operations. `FindTextInFiles` executes in a blocking task to prevent UI latency and skips `node_modules` and hidden directories, capping results at 1,000 matches. All handlers adhere to the project's strict PascalCase naming conventions and use the `ActionEffect`-style error mapping via Tonic `Status`.\n\nThis completes the foundational IPC contract for file manipulation, enabling the extension host to manage the workspace file system asynchronously.",
			"SHA": "8fe163e746245e5d7b978936215bb35438ab7c90"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T06:32:28Z",
